.TH LT-QWWAD_EF_INFINITE_WELL "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_ef_infinite_well (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_ef_infinite_well \- compute eigenstates in an infinite quantum well
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_ef_infinite_well
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find the eigenstates of an infinite quantum well.
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.HP
\fB\-L\fR [ \fB\-\-wellwidth\fR ] arg (=100) Width of quantum well [angstrom].
.TP
\fB\-m\fR [ \fB\-\-mass\fR ] arg (=0.067)
Effective mass (relative to free electron).
.TP
\fB\-N\fR [ \fB\-\-nz\fR ] arg (=100)
Number of spatial points for output file.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR [ \fB\-\-nst\fR ] arg (=1)
Number of states to find.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR [ \fB\-\-particle\fR ] arg (=e)
ID of particle to be used: 'e', 'h' or 'l', for
electrons, heavy holes or light holes
respectively.
.TP
\fB\-\-vcb\fR arg (=0)
Band\-edge potential [eV]
.TP
\fB\-\-alpha\fR arg (=0)
Non\-parabolicity parameter [eV^{\-1}]
.TP
\fB\-\-Ecutoff\fR arg
Cut\-off energy for solutions [meV]
.TP
\fB\-\-barrierwidth\fR arg (=0)
Width of barriers [angstrom]
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES

.SS Output files:
   'E*.r'    Energy of each state:
             Column 1: state index.
             Column 2: energy [meV].

   'wf_*i.r' Wave function amplitude at each position:
             Column 1: position [m].
             Column 2: wave function amplitude [m^{-1/2}].

In each case, the '*' is replaced by the particle ID and the 'i' is replaced by the number of the state.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compute the ground state in a 150-angstrom well with effective mass = 0.1m0:
   qwwad_ef_infinite_well --wellwidth 150 --mass 0.1
                        
Compute the first three heavy-hole states in a 200-angstrom well, using effective mass = 0.62m0:
   qwwad_ef_infinite_well --wellwidth 200 --mass 0.62 --particle h

Compute the ground state in a 100-angstrom well and "pad" the computed wave functions with 100-angstrom barriers:
   qwwad_ef_infinite_well --wellwidth 100 --barrierwidth 100
